{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-no-effort-high-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:04:39.748Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"01aea9461750554ca9fcf6c291b173670489a07294e0e3e795e8f77c105fff2c","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning that it was fixed. The same note also asks for the kiosk logs to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea opened it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 support for firmware testing.\n\nThe two numbers are written in different formats, and the issues sound different, so they look like separate tickets. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell whether #4419 is still open.\n\nWhat I left out:\n- **The other Moss notes about Quarrendon have no ticket numbers.** That's the 9/14/2025 pipeline digest, which only says your freight account \"needs a follow-up\", and the 3/23/2026 renewal note.\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882 are not Quarrendon.** They're in Moss's Central handoff note, but they belong to Central team accounts.\n- **Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note is about a different company.** It's spelled with one \"r\" and isn't a customer.\n\nI checked Moss's shared notes and digests only, not Slack messages."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
